L026 two-case template helper
============================

``prepare_l026_batch.py`` reads two case descriptors supplied by Root. It
does not select rows, read Original witness or status bytes, import numerical
Source, run a worker, or create true authority. The resulting FALSE files
must not be passed off as an issued call. Existing row304 files stay intact.

The cases file is a JSON list of exactly two dictionaries, each with
``free_index``, ``owner``, and ``witness_row_sha256``. Indices must be distinct,
in increasing order, and greater than304. This syntax check does not prove
that either row is unpaid or that its owner/hash is the actual Original row.
Root must establish those facts and exclude a repeated identical trial.
The helper also accepts Root's typed identity-selection result directly,
using its cases and checking its snapshot/witness descriptors against the
current metadata. It does not execute that selection or inspect its payload
sources. The result must have schema ROOT_L026_UNPAID_ROW_IDENTITY_SELECTION_V1.

An invocation has the following data-only shape (CASE_FILE must already be
prepared by Root; OUTPUT_DIRECTORY and both private runtime paths are fresh):

  python -E -B -S census/prepare_l026_batch.py --cases CASE_FILE
    --out OUTPUT_DIRECTORY --guard-output /private/tmp/UNUSED_GUARD_PATH
    --numerical-output /private/tmp/UNUSED_NUMERICAL_PATH

The output parent must already exist inside census. No execution is proposed
here for the placeholder paths, and no actual case identities are supplied.

